      <Comment source="pmngroup">Uridine ribohydrolase, a critical enzyme for uridine degradation, has only been recently cloned from Arabidopsis An &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; assay with the recombinant protein revealed that |FRAME: URIDINE uridine| is the preferred substrate CITS: [19293370]|. . |FRAME: XANTHOSINE xanthosine| was also somewhat favored with a maximal catalytic activity only about 6-fold lower than for |FRAME: URIDINE uridine| |CITS: [21235647]|. |FRAME: INOSINE Inosine| was hydrolyzed at a much lower rate, and |FRAME: ADENOSINE adenosine| was even less effective as a substrate. NSH1/URH1 can also act on methyluridine |CITS:[21235647]|. |FRAME: CYTIDINE Cytidine| was not metabolized as a substrate |CITS: [19293370]|. Arabidopsis NSH1 over-expression mutants have an increased capability to degrade imported |FRAME: URIDINE uridine|. miRNA- repressed mutants had decreased ability to degrade |FRAME: URIDINE uridine| |CITS: [19293370]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G36310-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G36310.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Panther" value="PTHR12304" />
